From 05c469a40b98d769f416739061add0468c20a84d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:42:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: advertise and use subgroups in the vertex stage

Metal rejects the SIMD-group attributes ([[thread_index_in_simdgroup]],
[[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]], [[threads_per_simdgroup]],
[[simdgroups_per_threadgroup]]) in a vertex function, but accepts every
SIMD-group function there. KosmicKrisp declared gl_SubGroupInvocation as such
an input, so a vertex shader that reads the lane id could not be compiled at
all (36 of the 38 pipelines of a shipped D3D12 title that vkd3d-proton turns
into vertex-stage wave ops failed to build).

Declare the four system values as locals in a vertex function instead: the lane
id is recovered from simd_ballot(true) and simd_prefix_exclusive_sum(1) over
the active lanes (clearing that many low bits off the ballot leaves this
invocation's own bit, whose index is the lane id; a fully active SIMD group
already has its lane id in the scan), the SIMD group size is Metal's fixed 32,
and gl_SubGroupID / gl_NumSubGroups are 0 and 1, because a vertex invocation
belongs to no workgroup. VERTEX is added to subgroupSupportedStages.

Tested with host/moltenvk/repro/wave_vertex.c: 96 vertices over three full SIMD
groups plus a 3-vertex tail draw, with the lane ids, ballot masks and exclusive
scans cross-checked against each other.

Generated-by: LLM
